#N canvas 270 120 764 560 12;
#X text 20 10 placed_sound <name>: an uploaded sound placed in the world \, played with array_player~ (loops). The sound itself is an array pair in main.pd's [pd sound_bank]. JS sends "set <left> [<right>]" and "distance <tiles> <radius>" to <name>-whistle-sound. Each time the sound has played through \, it says so on <name>-whistle-sound-end (JS ends a play-once sound). Close to the sound it plays slowly \, far away fast. (placed_sound_paulstretch_example.pd: the paulstretch~ version.);
#X obj 20 160 r \$1-whistle-sound;
#X obj 20 190 route set distance;
#X obj 20 220 list prepend set;
#X obj 20 250 list trim;
#X obj 20 450 array_player~;
#X obj 20 500 outlet~;
#X obj 100 500 outlet~;
#X obj 300 500 s \$1-whistle-sound-end;
#X obj 300 230 expr if(\$f2 > 0 \, \$f1 / \$f2 \, 0);
#X obj 300 260 moving_average 10;
#X obj 300 290 expr 0.5 * pow(4 \, min(1 \, max(0 \, \$f1)));
#X msg 300 320 rate \$1;
#X text 300 345 distance / radius (0 at the sound \, 1 at the edge) \, averaged over the last 10 values (about 0.8 s \, so it follows a little late) -> rate: 0 -> 0.5x \, 0.5 -> 1x \, 1 -> 2x;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 2 1 9 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 5 1 7 0;
#X connect 5 2 8 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 5 0;
